gains is attributable to periods prior to or during such <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">non-U.S.</FONT> holder&#8217;s ownership of our common stock. In addition, a repurchase of our common stock, to the extent not treated as a sale or exchange,
may be subject to withholding as an ordinary dividend. If a <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">non-U.S.</FONT> holder is subject to taxation under FIRPTA on proceeds from the sale of our common stock or on distributions we make, the <FONT
