our officers the power, in accordance with the general authorization, to fix the amount and other terms of the distribution. </P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Distributions in kind shall not be permitted, except for distributions of readily marketable securities, distributions of beneficial interests
in a liquidating trust established for our dissolution and the liquidation of our assets in accordance with the terms of our charter or distributions in which (a)&nbsp;our board of directors advises each stockholder of the risks associated with
direct ownership of the property, (b)&nbsp;our board of directors offers each stockholder the election of receiving such <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">in-kind</FONT> distributions, and <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">(c)&nbsp;in-kind</FONT>
